{
  "dom_id": "step-q62054",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The daily milk production on Debbie's farm has decreased at a rate of $12%$ every month. If the daily milk production was $1\\,130$ liters initially, then which function correctly represents $p(t),$ the daily milk production after $t$ months?",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is\n\n$$\np(t)=a(1-r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=1\\,130$ is the initial daily milk production.\n\n- $r=0.12$ is the decay rate ($12%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in months.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $p$ is\n\n$$\np(t)=1\\,130\\cdot (1-0.12)^{t}=1\\,130\\cdot (0.88)^{t}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
